{"title":"2017 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Visual_Roots_of_Unity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Visual Roots of Unity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> different complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d557abc96ef5645714518cb85cdfe172fc7273e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{24}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />. For how many of these is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7106dbd058b0b498357412899776516a95b9a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> a real number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/289cb30a8689be6853d6c4373080b584498105a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"367\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d557abc96ef5645714518cb85cdfe172fc7273e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{24}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0ab7246f1fbac4aaece41f78c056008feba13f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{\\frac{ni\\pi}{12}}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"17\" /> for integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee805b70af45e6662c40274ea0a0cc712fd32044.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq n&lt;24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />. So\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/a/8ca9e170bfba50d0e8b7f3a68f53669c18e27598.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6=e^{\\frac{ni\\pi}{2}}$\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>This is real if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/886398fe5e786f59e0f74dc564cf5e7cd98038af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{2}\\in \\mathbb{Z} \\Leftrightarrow (n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"94\" height=\"33\" /> is even<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/85852dfb3301b06f35017d1598f80915cce9a9ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"5\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, the answer is the number of even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee805b70af45e6662c40274ea0a0cc712fd32044.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq n&lt;24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcd831667ce2ed63775c6ccf9073c587604aec11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)=\\ 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"89\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/4060c4913d436489aa0d9801d50b7de6a677eee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\sqrt[24]{1} = 1^{\\frac{1}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euler%27s_identity\" title=\"Euler&#39;s identity\">Euler's identity</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa9df0f9646313d5a26679a4167a49aee96a87f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = e^{0 \\times i} = \\cos (0+2k\\pi) + i \\sin(0+2k\\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"316\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer.\n</p><p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Moivre%27s_Theorem\" title=\"De Moivre&#39;s Theorem\">De Moivre's Theorem</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49bc4d3ca55bbb431fdc9ec494e596215990b2f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 1^{\\frac{1}{24}} = {\\cos (\\frac{k\\pi}{12}) + i \\sin (\\frac{k\\pi}{12})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"238\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e12ecb2330aa467078d8d06dc0d435c3882a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq k&lt;24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> that produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> unique results.\n</p><p>Using De Moivre's Theorem again, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/3400a7919a098078a28785d6ebf06d3d9b5481b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6 = {\\cos (\\frac{k\\pi}{2}) + i \\sin (\\frac{k\\pi}{2})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"196\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7106dbd058b0b498357412899776516a95b9a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> to be real, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0fbb0de7701a08c8639924a96d5a22c17ecc9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\frac{k\\pi}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> has to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to negate the imaginary component. This occurs whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18205c5a2f5ef1d7294be718b6aee8eeaba9567.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> is an integer multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, requiring that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is even. There are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/38693a75a9e00c962455566cda9d06d94da1738b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> even values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e12ecb2330aa467078d8d06dc0d435c3882a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq k&lt;24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de641a309fc5878c26baf699f2382b7d4b02b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the start, recall from the Fundamental Theorem of Algebra that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2ec0dd00b0822202787cd8c58b56972e607af79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{24} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> solutions (and these must be distinct since the equation factors into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57d39fe27d2cf2d2ccffd0fd59e42980554de271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = (z-1)(z^{23} + z^{22} + z^{21}... + z + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"293\" height=\"19\" />), or notice that the question is simply referring to the 24th roots of unity, of which we know there must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ff26f03bdf71a6bc20a9a5b166cb1f3a3aaec00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = z^{24} = (z^6)^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"19\" />, so for any solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7106dbd058b0b498357412899776516a95b9a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> will be one of the 4th roots of unity (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fda51aabf3fa68a72ba3b46518abc175c76dab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-i$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />). Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> will satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/728eaf9a93a6a111a69ede7008d2959ecb91ded8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929d561188c1d4a191c240422acf81986c6144cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> (and this is further justified by knowledge of the 6th roots of unity), so there must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d985dba1770e9e2e805dc4acf8b8ed54902acca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D) \\: 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"63\" height=\"29\" /> such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Quick)\">Solution 4 (Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022940a765ca072793b00931ceecd0f1a8a073f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2ac0112f46cc7025a8e8b6b62fd610e3f4c18f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = z^6.$\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a997d4837f2bc68d2d249a020d83fe2ae50f07e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^4 = 1 \\implies a = 1,-1.\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edba30dd8568ec3a3515d06d660bd4fc8bc371f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6 = \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> has 6 solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> respectively, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed9d170dc49c03508abd08a3a0e30bf5b3c5005e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+6=\\boxed{(D)\\ 12}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"133\" height=\"29\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f1406b65f9f2e6a365b7356da731780b42cceb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\]\" />\n-svyn\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Visual_Roots_of_Unity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Visual_Roots_of_Unity)\">Solution 5 (Visual Roots of Unity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Visual Roots of Unity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2ec0dd00b0822202787cd8c58b56972e607af79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{24} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, we can plot these points on the Argand plane as a regular 24-gon, as shown: \n<span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2017AMC12aP17.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/4e/2017AMC12aP17.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"952\" height=\"908\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\nThese are a graphical representation of all 24 values of z, as stated in the problem. Now, we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7106dbd058b0b498357412899776516a95b9a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> to be real. The only 2 cases where this happens are if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/728eaf9a93a6a111a69ede7008d2959ecb91ded8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929d561188c1d4a191c240422acf81986c6144cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />. Squaring both sides for the latter equation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df2956a46bd5ec7e5f7b20003051c0b7fab2980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{12}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" />, which, if one were to square root it, would give us a system of both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/728eaf9a93a6a111a69ede7008d2959ecb91ded8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929d561188c1d4a191c240422acf81986c6144cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />, just as we desire. We can plot the points for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df2956a46bd5ec7e5f7b20003051c0b7fab2980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{12}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" /> on an Argand plane again, giving us: \n<span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2017AMC12aP17-p2.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/83/2017AMC12aP17-p2.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1000\" height=\"922\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\nWe note that all of these points are also on the first Argand plane, and counting the points nets us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4385eeae6eab5c036bd49e9bfe9bcb47290373.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)\\ 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"32\" /> total values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f1406b65f9f2e6a365b7356da731780b42cceb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\]\" />\n-yingkai_0_ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f1406b65f9f2e6a365b7356da731780b42cceb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\]\" />\nCredit to Michael Andrejkovics for providing the GeoGebra widget used to make these diagrams!\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_.28English-Chinese_Bilingual.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\">Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/N69icKTqOoU\">https://youtu.be/N69icKTqOoU</a>\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A\">2017 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2017 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\